Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:00:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 028/147] mobile: leaving a session forgets the button presses
 it sent

InputModel records the mouse buttons sendMouse pressed, so that only the
release of one of them uses up a one-shot key-bar modifier. The phone reuses
one InputModel for every session, and resetModifiers(), which FFI.close()
calls, cleared the modifiers but not that record. A session that ended with
a button held (the connection dropped during a touch-mode drag) left the
press behind: in the next session the spare release a pinch ends with
matched it and used up an armed Shift or Ctrl, which a pinch to aim must not
do.

resetModifiers() now clears the record too. On a desktop the key bar has no
one-shot modifiers, so clearing it there changes nothing.

(Release 1.5.1 review, dart-behavior finding 8.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/lib/models/input_model.dart | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/flutter/lib/models/input_model.dart b/flutter/lib/models/input_model.dart
index ac01ea4..6f2f26d 100644
--- a/flutter/lib/models/input_model.dart
+++ b/flutter/lib/models/input_model.dart
@@ -1187,6 +1187,7 @@ class InputModel {
   void resetModifiers() {
     shift = ctrl = alt = command = false;
     keyBarModifiers.clear();
+    _sentButtonPresses.clear();
   }
 
   /// Modify the given modifier map [evt] based on current modifier key status.
